56 number and model details.\n2. The Rita et al. paper (arXiv:2409.08792) - to find the 34.53 and their protocol details.\n3. The facebookresearch/gismo GitHub repo - for code and config details.\n\nLet me also check the Rita paper more carefully for what differs in their reimplementation (they say \"The original GISMo model was trained in this dataset using a methodology focused on ingredient context and co-occurrence\" and \"Running the GISMo model five times ... yielded Hit@1 accuracies of 34.53 ± 0.10%\").\n\nKey question: why does Rita get 34.53 while Meta reports ~20.56? The option lists possible causes: data split, candidate set, preprocessing.\n\nI recall that the GISMo paper's eval uses the \"candidate set\" of 1,000 (?) most common ingredients or similar. Actually, let me look at the GISMo code/paper.\n\nLet me fetch these pages."
