    "content": " \\[2302.07960\\] Learning to Substitute Ingredients in Recipes                               \n\n[Skip to main content](#content)\n\n[](https://arxiv.org/IgnoreMe)[![archive](/static/base/1.0.1/images/arxiv-logo-primary-light.svg)](https://arxiv.org/)\n\n[Search](https://arxiv.org/search) [Submit](https://arxiv.org/user/create) [Donate](https://info.arxiv.org/about/donate.html) [Log in](https://arxiv.org/login)\n\nSearch arXiv   \n\nPress Enter to search · [Advanced search](https://arxiv.org/search/advanced)\n\n# Computer Science > Machine Learning\n\n**arXiv:2302.07960** (cs)\n\n\\[Submitted on 15 Feb 2023\\]\n\n# Title:Learning to Substitute Ingredients in Recipes\n\nAuthors:[Bahare Fatemi](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Fatemi,+B), [Quentin Duval](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Duval,+Q), [Rohit Girdhar](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Girdhar,+R), [Michal Drozdzal](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Drozdzal,+M), [Adriana Romero-Soriano](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Romero-Soriano,+A)\n\nView a PDF of the paper titled Learning to Substitute Ingredients in Recipes, by Bahare Fatemi and 4 other authors\n\n[View PDF](/pdf/2302.07960) [HTML (experimental)](https://arxiv.org/html/2302.07960v1)\n\n> Abstract:Recipe personalization through ingredient substitution has the potential to help people meet their dietary needs and preferences, avoid potential allergens, and ease culinary exploration in everyone's kitchen. To address ingredient substitution, we build a benchmark, composed of a dataset of substitution pairs with standardized splits, evaluation metrics, and baselines. We further introduce Graph-based Ingredient Substitution Module (GISMo), a novel model that leverages the context of a recipe as well as generic ingredient relational information encoded within a graph to rank plausible substitutions. We show through comprehensive experimental validation that GISMo surpasses the best performing baseline by a large margin in terms of mean reciprocal rank. Finally, we highlight the benefits of GISMo by integrating it in an improved image-to-recipe generation pipeline, enabling recipe personalization through user intervention. Quantitative and qualitative results show the efficacy of our proposed system, paving the road towards truly personalized cooking and tasting experiences.\n\nSubjects:\n\nMachine Learning (cs.LG); Human-Computer Interaction (cs.HC)\n\nCite as:\n\n[arXiv:2302.07960](https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.07960) \\[cs.LG\\]\n\n \n\n(or [arXiv:2302.07960v1](https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.07960v1) \\[cs.LG\\] for this version)\n\n \n\n[https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2302.07960](https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2302.07960)\n\nFocus to learn more\n\narXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\n\n## Submission history\n\nFrom: Bahare Fatemi \\[[view email](/show-email/7f616713/2302.07960)\\]  \n**\\[v1\\]** Wed, 15 Feb 2023 21:49:23 UTC (22,681 KB)  \n\nFull-text links:\n\n## Access Paper:\n\nView a PDF of the paper titled Learning to Substitute Ingredients in Recipes, by Bahare Fatemi and 4 other authors\n\n-   [View PDF](/pdf/2302.07960)\n-   [HTML (experimental)](https://arxiv.org/html/2302.07960v1)\n-   [TeX Source](/src/2302.07960)\n\n[view license](http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/ \"Rights to this article\")\n\n### Current browse context:\n\ncs.LG\n\n[< prev](/prevnext?id=2302.07960&function=prev&context=cs.LG \"previous in cs.LG (accesskey p)\")   |   [next >](/prevnext?id=2302.07960&function=next&context=cs.LG \"next in cs.LG (accesskey n)\")  \n\n[new](/list/cs.LG/new) | [recent](/list/cs.LG/recent) | [2023-02](/list/cs.LG/2023-02)\n\nChange to browse by:\n\n[cs](/abs/2302.07960?context=cs)  \n[cs.HC](/abs/2302.07960?context=cs.HC)  \n\n### References & Citations\n\n-   [NASA ADS](https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/arXiv:2302.07960)\n-   [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?arxiv